# Dialtone is the design system

All UI should look like Dialtone. Vue Dialtone components are optional; **tokens and utility classes are not**.

## Do

- Use `--dt-*` tokens from `src/assets/design-tokens.css` for color, space, type, radius, and shadows.
- Use Dialtone `d-*` utility classes in markup. Prefer official names from [dialtone.dialpad.com](https://dialtone.dialpad.com/).
- If a token or utility is missing locally, look it up on the Dialtone site, then add a local replica to `design-tokens.css` or `utilities.css`. Do not invent values.
- If you must write custom CSS, still use `--dt-*` tokens (never raw hex/px for design values). Prefer padding + gap over margin.

## Don’t

- Do not install `@dialpad/dialtone`, `@dialpad/dialtone-css`, `@dialpad/dialtone-icons`, or `@dialpad/dialtone-tokens`.
- Do not hardcode colors, spacing, or type that Dialtone already tokens.

Lookup index and naming: [DESIGN.md](DESIGN.md).
